##############################################################################
                             REQUIRED REFERENCES
##############################################################################

 Description of the relativistic four-component DFT method for calculation
 of hyperfine coupling constants is presented for the first time in Ref [1].
 In addition this work studies effects of finite size model for both charge
 and magnetic moment distributions on the hyperfine structure of heavy nuclei.

 [1] E. Malkin, M. Repisky, S. Komorovsky, P. Mach, O.L. Malkina,
     and V.G. Malkin, J. Chem. Phys. 134, 044111 (2011).
     [DOI: https://doi.org/10.1063/1.3526263]

 XCFun: a library of DFT exchange-correlation functionals

 [2] U. Ekström, et al., J. Chem. Theory Comput. 6, 1971-1980 (2010)
     [DOI: https://doi.org/10.1021/ct100117s]


